WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:02.884
- Am I gonna shove more
hot dog down this gullet?

00:00:02.884 --> 00:00:05.371
You can bet my sweet,
fine (beep) you will.

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:07.954
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.892 --> 00:00:11.752
- We are in Chicago, Illinois.

00:00:11.752 --> 00:00:12.585
- That's right.

00:00:12.585 --> 00:00:13.959
- Known for a couple of things,

00:00:13.959 --> 00:00:16.858
its sport teams and "hat dawgz."

00:00:16.858 --> 00:00:17.940
- Our good friend, Annie,

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:18.883
behind the camera right there,

00:00:18.883 --> 00:00:21.644
was like, "Why don't we try
the top three places on Yelp

00:00:21.644 --> 00:00:24.131
"and see if they're actually
as good as they say they are.

00:00:24.131 --> 00:00:25.609
"Cause Yelp is a very powerful tool

00:00:25.609 --> 00:00:27.691
"that a lot of people
use to find restaurants."

00:00:27.691 --> 00:00:28.554
Here's the thing though.

00:00:28.554 --> 00:00:30.341
It sometimes is an unfair way

00:00:30.341 --> 00:00:33.339
that does very strongly
affect small businesses.

00:00:33.339 --> 00:00:35.008
- And it's very subjective, too.

00:00:35.008 --> 00:00:36.731
- Yeah, take everything on
Yelp with a grain of salt.

00:00:36.731 --> 00:00:40.006
- A Chicago style hot dog
is poppy or sesame bun,

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:44.172
yellow mustard, onions,
relish, tomatoes, hot peppers,

00:00:44.172 --> 00:00:46.963
a long pickle, and that's usually it.

00:00:46.963 --> 00:00:49.223
It's very simple and really
there's never ketchup

00:00:49.223 --> 00:00:50.056
(buzzer noise) on there.

00:00:50.056 --> 00:00:50.922
- What?
- No ketchup.

00:00:50.922 --> 00:00:53.391
- No? What if I'm running behind?

00:00:53.391 --> 00:00:55.028
(Steven laughing)
- All right.

00:00:55.028 --> 00:00:56.083
That's brilliant. That's it.

00:00:56.083 --> 00:00:57.352
That's all we need!

00:00:57.352 --> 00:00:58.554
You got it! Bye!

00:00:58.554 --> 00:01:01.054
(tango music)

00:01:08.641 --> 00:01:09.829
- We're at Fatso's!

00:01:09.829 --> 00:01:12.189
One thing about Fatso's is
that their dogs are charred

00:01:12.189 --> 00:01:13.022
on the grill.

00:01:13.022 --> 00:01:14.511
They're a little bit
crispier than I think your--

00:01:14.511 --> 00:01:15.913
- Crispier.
- Average hot dog.

00:01:15.913 --> 00:01:17.049
- They're a little burnt on the end.

00:01:17.049 --> 00:01:17.974
- Yeah, they're a little burnt.

00:01:17.974 --> 00:01:19.515
- A little smokey.
- A little smokey.

00:01:19.515 --> 00:01:20.864
- You know? Look at that dog.

00:01:20.864 --> 00:01:22.236
- Yeah.
- It's pretty big.

00:01:22.236 --> 00:01:23.184
- One hot diggidy-dog.

00:01:23.184 --> 00:01:26.242
- Cheers.
- Sesame seed bun.

00:01:26.242 --> 00:01:28.161
I think the char actually
gives it a little bit

00:01:28.161 --> 00:01:30.656
more of a extra flavor which I appreciate.

00:01:30.656 --> 00:01:32.335
- This is a dangerous place, okay?

00:01:32.335 --> 00:01:33.919
If I lived right on this corner,

00:01:33.919 --> 00:01:35.935
I'd probably be eating
here at least once a week.

00:01:35.935 --> 00:01:37.357
- They gave us a lot of fries.

00:01:37.357 --> 00:01:39.888
This thing is overflowing with onions.

00:01:39.888 --> 00:01:41.214
- We typed in "Fatso's" right?

00:01:41.214 --> 00:01:42.972
And I was like, "Ah,
this can't be that good."

00:01:42.972 --> 00:01:44.767
Four and a half stars, though, on Yelp,

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:46.613
which is not too shabby.

00:01:46.613 --> 00:01:47.579
- Good hot dog.

00:01:47.579 --> 00:01:48.500
- It's a good hot dog.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:49.333
- More hot dogs!

00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:51.554
- Annie, why did I do this?

00:01:51.554 --> 00:01:52.934
This is your fault.

00:01:52.934 --> 00:01:53.897
- [Annie] Don't point at me.

00:01:53.897 --> 00:01:56.314
(jazz music)

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:05.073
- All right. This is spot number two.

00:02:05.073 --> 00:02:06.129
We're at U.B. Dogs

00:02:06.129 --> 00:02:08.445
and we got their Chicago hot dog.

00:02:08.445 --> 00:02:09.775
- This is their joey dog.

00:02:09.775 --> 00:02:10.608
- Their joey.

00:02:10.608 --> 00:02:11.993
It is a very beautiful dog.

00:02:11.993 --> 00:02:14.620
- Yeah, the joey dog is
pretty intense looking.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:15.745
- All right, so here's yours.

00:02:15.745 --> 00:02:17.345
- Thanks, I already know
I'm gonna love this.

00:02:17.345 --> 00:02:19.156
This is the hot dog I ate
all the time growing up.

00:02:19.156 --> 00:02:20.504
It's why I never put
ketchup on my hot dog.

00:02:20.504 --> 00:02:21.498
It's weird.

00:02:21.498 --> 00:02:22.619
- This looks really good actually.

00:02:22.619 --> 00:02:25.783
- Yeah, it's gonna be dope!
- Cheers.

00:02:25.783 --> 00:02:26.717
Oh, that pepper kick!

00:02:26.717 --> 00:02:28.656
- There's a little bit of
spice to these hot dogs.

00:02:28.656 --> 00:02:31.924
All of the condiments
are expertly seasoned.

00:02:31.924 --> 00:02:34.085
- Oh yeah, it is really good.

00:02:34.085 --> 00:02:35.867
Two hot dogs and a drink and fries

00:02:35.867 --> 00:02:38.384
for under $10 is a very good deal.

00:02:38.384 --> 00:02:39.217
- [Jen] Yeah.

00:02:39.217 --> 00:02:40.345
- So, I'll give them props for that.

00:02:40.345 --> 00:02:41.178
- A little soggy bun.

00:02:41.178 --> 00:02:42.719
Sometimes I like them
a little bit crispier,

00:02:42.719 --> 00:02:44.585
but all in all, a pretty decent dog.

00:02:44.585 --> 00:02:45.886
- Here's the thing, if I wanted a hot dog

00:02:45.886 --> 00:02:47.205
and I looked on Yelp
and I found this place

00:02:47.205 --> 00:02:49.145
and I came here, I would be satisfied.

00:02:49.145 --> 00:02:50.786
- I want ketchup on this.

00:02:50.786 --> 00:02:51.714
- [Jen] Annie!

00:02:51.714 --> 00:02:54.131
(jazz music)

00:02:58.689 --> 00:03:01.532
- Okay. The number one rated place on Yelp

00:03:01.532 --> 00:03:03.591
for hot dogs in Chicago.

00:03:03.591 --> 00:03:04.578
It's pretty small.

00:03:04.578 --> 00:03:05.411
- Mm-hmm.

00:03:05.411 --> 00:03:06.717
- I do love the logo.

00:03:06.717 --> 00:03:07.745
The mascot?

00:03:07.745 --> 00:03:08.741
- It's pretty cute.
- It's cute.

00:03:08.741 --> 00:03:10.329
That is an immense pickle.

00:03:10.329 --> 00:03:15.219
It's not as photogenic as
you would expect it to be.

00:03:15.219 --> 00:03:19.157
- It is a very unique
experience eating this hot dog.

00:03:19.157 --> 00:03:20.378
- I actually think the meat

00:03:20.378 --> 00:03:22.092
on this hot dog is more flavorful.

00:03:22.092 --> 00:03:24.918
- It's memorable cause
that bite is just like

00:03:24.918 --> 00:03:27.055
all of this pickle coming in.

00:03:27.055 --> 00:03:28.403
- I actually really do like it.

00:03:28.403 --> 00:03:29.236
- You do like it?

00:03:29.236 --> 00:03:30.287
- Yeah, I like it a lot.

00:03:30.287 --> 00:03:33.029
It is the least attractive
hot dog we've seen.

00:03:33.029 --> 00:03:34.412
(Annie laughing)

00:03:34.412 --> 00:03:35.886
No offense, it's kind of ugly.
- [Steven] It's true.

00:03:35.886 --> 00:03:37.580
- But I think this was
my favorite hot dog.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:38.994
- Whoa! I can't believe it.

00:03:38.994 --> 00:03:40.013
- It was the nostalgia factor

00:03:40.013 --> 00:03:41.251
that really brought it home for me.

00:03:41.251 --> 00:03:42.561
- I'm gonna probably go with U.B.'s.

00:03:42.561 --> 00:03:46.354
It was just bursting with
ingredients and flavor.

00:03:46.354 --> 00:03:47.410
- Yeah.
- Yeah, it was really good.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:49.116
- I'm bursting with
something, too, over here,

00:03:49.116 --> 00:03:49.949
you know what I mean?

00:03:49.949 --> 00:03:53.415
But I'm not sure you
can have a favorite one

00:03:53.415 --> 00:03:56.832
when at the end of it you do want to die.

00:04:05.677 --> 00:04:07.010
There's a train.

00:04:12.514 --> 00:04:13.347
- [Annie] Okay.

00:04:13.347 --> 00:04:14.180
- [Steven] You're gross.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:15.930
- [Jen] I feel awful.

